---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Data Converter privacy policy — we do not collect, store, or share your data. Everything runs in your browser." keywords="privacy policy, data privacy, browser-based, no upload" breadcrumbs={[{name:'Home',url:'/'},{name:'Privacy',url:'/privacy'}]} schema={{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy Policy',
  description: 'Data Converter does not collect, store, or share your data. All processing happens in your browser.',
  about: { '@type': 'Thing', name: 'Privacy' },
}}>
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><em>Last updated: July 2026</em></p>

    <h2>What This Covers</h2>
    <p>This privacy policy explains how Data Converter ("we", "I", "this site") handles your information when you use the tools on this website.</p>

    <h2>No Data Collection</h2>
    <p>All file conversion, parsing, and processing happens entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your data — whether you paste it, upload it, or fetch it from a URL — never leaves your device. I don't have servers that receive or store your files.</p>

    <h2>No Accounts, No Tracking</h2>
    <p>You don't need an account to use this tool. I don't use analytics scripts that track your behavior across sites without your consent. The only analytics I run is Google Analytics with basic page view data (no user-level tracking), which helps me understand which features people use most.</p>

    <h2>Cookies &amp; Consent</h2>
    <p>I use minimal cookies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A cookie to remember your theme preference (light/dark mode). This is strictly functional and always set.</li>
      <li>Google Analytics uses its own cookies for aggregate page view statistics — only loaded after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
      <li>Google AdSense sets cookies for ad delivery and personalization — only loaded after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Non-essential scripts (analytics and ads) are blocked until you click "Got it" on the cookie banner. Your choice is saved locally so the banner doesn't reappear. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>

    <h2>External Services</h2>
    <p>If you use the <strong>URL Fetch</strong> feature with the CORS proxy enabled, your request routes through a third-party proxy service. That service sees the URL you request but not your personal information. The CORS proxy is off by default.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, I'll update the date at the top. I'll also post a notice on the site for significant changes.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 40px auto;
    padding: 0 16px;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
  }
  .legal em {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 550;
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .legal p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal li {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal { margin: 24px auto; }
    .legal h1 { font-size: 24px; }
  }
</style>
